            <div xml:id="d414">

                <pb facs="0586" n="490" sameAs="frus:frus1921v02/pg490"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">812.52/619: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Chargé in Mexico</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Hanna</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1921-05-14T17:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">May 14, 1921—5
                                p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>65. Your despatch 3847, April 30th, Agrarian Bill.<anchor n="97" xml:id="d414-f1"
                    /></p>
                <p>Consulate San Luis Potosi reports Bill has passed and Act now in force.</p>
                <pb facs="0587" n="491" xml:id="pg491"/>
                <p>Informally request appropriate authorities to advise you whether such is the case
                    and take occasion to renew informal protest made pursuant Department’s 54, April
                    20th, 6 p.m., adding that this Government will not consent to the application of
                    the attempted confiscatory provisions of this measure to American citizens
                    owning land acquired in accordance with Mexican law.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hughes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
